{"content":[{"c":["MOREH, Oak of"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Abraham’s first recorded stopping place upon entering Palestine after leaving Mesopotamia. Here he built an altar to God (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.12.6","r":"Gen.12.6","rawR":"Gen.12.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.12.6","value":"Gen.12.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 12:6"},"). Later, Moses mentioned this place as a geographical landmark to identify the whereabouts of Mt Gerizim and Mt Ebal (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.11.30","r":"Deut.11.30","rawR":"Deut.11.30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.11.30","value":"Deut.11.30"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 11:30"},"). The ",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," improperly reads “plain” of Moreh. The oak of Moreh was located near Shechem."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"MorehOakof","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 12:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.12.6","rawQueryValue":"Gen.12.6","sourceRefExact":"Gen.12.6"},{"anchorText":"Dt 11:30","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.11.30","rawQueryValue":"Deut.11.30","sourceRefExact":"Deut.11.30"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"067ea2e31d83d5b575fad7a86ee9cafed91f8c8be6f2a0c570120ee8f7c11d02","sourceItemName":"MorehOakof","sourceItemOrder":396,"sourceMember":"Articles/M.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"MorehOakof","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Moreh, Oak of","title":"Moreh, Oak of","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}